  "contribution": {
    "summary": "Qualify a new immutable, unpublished dw.quantities.standard calendar package carrying the six-unit opt-in Math electrochemical profile through an isolated exact PackageReference-only binary consumer.",
    "value": "Build the next unoccupied on-date Standard NuGet candidate from six source files with two exact published dependencies. Verify real ZIP/nuspec and all archive SHA-256 identities, load three matching compiled DLLs through an independent consumer, pass twelve named binary probes and record actual local restore sources.",
    "debtChanges": [
      "RS173 succeeded at attempt 001 after a single pre-attempt refusal: twelve Math-owned source tests passed and the six-unit opt-in profile was compiled, but no new package was qualified.",
      "Preserve published Standard [20260.20261103.1001], Quantities [20260.20261102.1001] and Expression [20260.20261102.1001] bytes, five original Standard sources, and exact direct dependencies.",
      "AURA code reuse rights remain unestablished. No AURA source, old catalogue, license/SPDX, shared feed or sibling repository is modified by this candidate-only gate.",
      "The independent package-only consumer operates against the candidate and exact old dependencies, not a published delivery; later owner-authorized immutable publication and independent physical-feed readback remain mandatory.",
      "RS174 first invocation failed pre-attempt with nested_repository_refused: the shared private-feed reader refuses unrelated child directories by default. The same run now explicitly selects nonrecursive top-level-only inventory with full package/hash checks."
    ],
    "nextAction": "Qualify an original-candidate-only immutable private publisher and publish only identical bytes into NUGET_LOCAL without overwrite under the U-N delivery authorization; independently re-read published archives and all three loaded DLLs.",
    "achievements": []
